# clangd config for libtetrissh — teaches the language server where the headers
# live. They sit in include/ (tetrissh.h, internal.h, libs/common.h), not beside
# the .c files, so without a hint clangd floods every source/test with bogus
# "file not found" errors on #include "tetrissh.h" / "libs/common.h". The
# Makefile passes -Iinclude, but clangd has no compile_commands database here, so
# it runs a generic fallback whose working directory is the *source file's own
# directory* (src/ or tests/). A plain -Iinclude would resolve to src/include
# (nonexistent); -I../include resolves to lib/libtetrissh/include for every .c
# under src/ and tests/ (all exactly one level deep), which also covers the
# libs/ subdir. Build flags are unchanged; this only affects the editor.
CompileFlags:
  Add:
    - -I../include
